{"url": "https://api.openalex.org/works?search=Evidence+of+spontaneous+complexity+increase+in+multi-agent+reinforcement+learning+systems+without+explicit+complexity+objectives.&per-page=4&select=id%2Cdoi%2Ctitle%2Cpublication_year%2Ctype%2Ccited_by_count%2Copen_access%2Cprimary_location%2Cabstract_inverted_index", "scope": "OpenAlex scholarly metadata and reconstructed abstracts where supplied; not full papers", "excerpt": "[{"id": "https://openalex.org/W4415901941", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.52202/085713-4567", "title": "A Principle of Targeted Intervention for Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning", "publication_year": 2025, "type": "conference-paper", "cited_by_count": 0, "open_access": {"is_oa": true, "oa_status": "green", "oa_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.17697", "any_repository_has_fulltext": true}, "primary_location": {"id": "doi:10.52202/085713-4567", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.52202/085713-4567", "is_oa": false, "landing_page_url": "https://doi.org/10.52202/085713-4567", "pdf_url": null, "source": {"id": "https://openalex.org/S4363606243", "display_name": "neural information processing systems", "issn_l": "1049-5258", "issn": ["1049-5258"], "is_oa": false, "is_in_doaj": false, "is_core": true, "listed_in": ["cwts-core", "norway-2"], "host_organization": null, "host_organization_name": null, "host_organization_lineage": [], "host_organization_lineage_names": [], "type": "conference"}, "license": null, "license_id": null, "version": "publishedVersion", "is_accepted": true, "is_published": true, "raw_source_name": "Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 38", "raw_type": "proceedings-article"}, "abstract": "Steering cooperative multi-agent reinforcement learning (MARL) towards desired outcomes is challenging, particularly when the global guidance from a human on the whole multi-agent system is impractical in a large-scale MARL. On the other hand, designing external mechanisms (e.g., intrinsic rewards and human feedback) to coordinate agents mostly relies on empirical studies, lacking a easy-to-use research tool. In this work, we employ multi-agent influence diagrams (MAIDs) as a graphical framework to address the above issues. First, we introduce the concept of MARL interaction paradigms (orthogonal to MARL learning paradigms), using MAIDs to analyze and visualize both unguided self-organization and global guidance mechanisms in MARL. Then, we design a new MARL interaction paradigm, referred to as the targeted intervention paradigm that is applied to only a single targeted agent, so the problem of global guidance can be mitigated. In implementation, we introduce a causal inference technique, referred to as Pre-Strategy Intervention (PSI), to realize the targeted intervention paradigm. Since MAIDs can be regarded as a special class of causal diagrams, a composite desired outcome that integrates the primary task goal and an additional desired outcome can be ac

